        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to empty both your draw pile and your discard pile.',
          gameplay: "1. Each player has a face-down draw pile and a face-up discard pile.\n2. In the center, four foundation piles (one for each suit) are built UPWARDS in suit.\n3. **Turn Action**: You must play cards from your draw/discard pile to the center OR onto an opponent's discard pile (if one rank higher, regardless of suit).\n4. **Forced Play**: If a card CAN be played to a center foundation, it MUST be played before any other move.\n5. **Juse!**: If a player misses a forced play, any other player can shout 'JUSE!'. The offender must take cards from the bottom of every other player's pile.",
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Juse.',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Scoring follows the game-specific point or pot rules.',
            'Winning condition: Be the first to empty both your draw pile and your discard pile.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Keep a very close eye on the center foundations. The moment a rank appears that you have on your discard pile, play it immediately. Speed is everything.',
          intermediate: "Offensive Filling: Use every opportunity to dump your cards onto your opponents' discard piles. This 'buries' their useful cards and gets you closer to winning.",
          advanced: "Trap Playing: If you have a card that could go to the center, but playing it would help your opponent more than you (e.g., they have the next card in sequence), try to delayâ€”but be careful not to get 'Juse'd'!",
          tips: [
            'Always check the center foundations before looking at your own draw pile.',
            'If you are about to play a card on an opponent, check if it could go to the center first. Foundation play is always priority.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
